WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.120
Hey everyone, привет, welcome to привет русский, Episode 35, for 6 июня 2026 года.

00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:10.440
I am allia. The day's lesson is going to be a fun one.

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:16.640
Поехали, our word of the day is mid-ведь, mid-ведь, say it slowly with me, mid-ведь.

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:21.760
It sounds like my yet-веда. Picture a big foreign, my yet-вед,

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:24.440
Lumbering through the forest like a walking teddy bear.

00:00:24.980 --> 00:00:28.420
Mid-ведь любит мёт, that means the bear likes honey.

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:30.300
Репит авторми, mid-ведь.

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:32.620
Now let's build more animal words.

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:35.080
Our first new word is собака.

00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:36.120
собака.

00:00:36.580 --> 00:00:38.460
It sounds like собака.

00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:40.000
собака means dog.

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:43.100
Imagine a dog with a sword like tail named собака.

00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:44.680
Репит авторми, собака.

00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:48.500
собака бежит быстро, that means the dog runs fast.

00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:50.660
Next comes кошка, кошка.

00:00:51.020 --> 00:00:52.500
It sounds like кошка.

00:00:52.740 --> 00:00:53.740
кошка means cat.

00:00:54.080 --> 00:00:56.740
кошка rhymes with cushion, because cats love cushions.

00:00:56.740 --> 00:00:58.580
Репит авторми, кошка.

00:00:59.240 --> 00:01:02.340
кошка спит надевания, that means the cat sleeps on the sofa.

00:01:02.820 --> 00:01:04.160
Now we have птица.

00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:06.420
птица, it sounds like птица.

00:01:06.700 --> 00:01:07.840
птица means bird.

00:01:08.180 --> 00:01:10.680
птица sounds just like tweet, which is what birds do.

00:01:11.140 --> 00:01:12.660
Репит авторми, птица.

00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:16.340
птица пойдет утром, that means the bird sings in the morning.

00:01:16.880 --> 00:01:18.640
Here is рыба, рыба.

00:01:19.040 --> 00:01:21.820
It sounds like рыба, рыба means fish.

00:01:22.340 --> 00:01:24.920
рыба sounds like river, because fish live in rivers.

00:01:24.920 --> 00:01:28.780
Репит авторми, рыба, рыба плавает в воде.

00:01:29.140 --> 00:01:31.060
That means the fish swims in the water.

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:33.600
Next is ложать, ложать.

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:35.520
It sounds like ложь-шад.

00:01:35.940 --> 00:01:36.820
ложь-шад means horse.

00:01:37.340 --> 00:01:39.980
ложь-шад sounds like lash-mado over horse's grace.

00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:42.100
Репит авторми, ложь-шад.

00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:45.280
ложь-шад есть траву, that means the horse eats grass.

00:01:45.880 --> 00:01:47.860
Now we meet zayatz, zayatz.

00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:51.560
It sounds like zayatz, zayatz means hair or rabbit.

00:01:51.560 --> 00:01:55.400
зayatz sounds like zaini, because hair's are zaini jumpers.

00:01:55.740 --> 00:01:59.120
Репит авторми, зayatz, зayatz, прыгает высоко.

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:01.200
That means the hair jumps high.

00:02:01.740 --> 00:02:03.080
Here is walk, walk.

00:02:03.580 --> 00:02:05.440
It sounds like walk, means wolf.

00:02:05.980 --> 00:02:09.420
Walk sounds like folk, because wolves appear in folk tales.

00:02:09.820 --> 00:02:13.080
Репит авторми, walk, walk живет в лесу.

00:02:13.540 --> 00:02:15.760
That means the wolf lives in the forest.

00:02:16.760 --> 00:02:19.720
Our last animal word is mush, mush.

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:22.920
It sounds like mush, mush means mouse.

00:02:23.460 --> 00:02:26.260
Mush sounds like mishes, because mice are mischievous.

00:02:26.620 --> 00:02:29.660
Репит авторми, мыш, мыш любит сыр.

00:02:30.020 --> 00:02:31.680
That means the mouse likes cheese.

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:34.760
Russian nouns have gender that change their endings.

00:02:35.440 --> 00:02:38.140
Медведь is masculine and often ends in a consonant.

00:02:38.620 --> 00:02:40.860
Кошка is feminine and ends in a.

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:44.860
English has almost no gender endings, but Russian does.

00:02:44.860 --> 00:02:47.320
Абит бер is большой медведь.

00:02:47.640 --> 00:02:49.580
Абит кат is большая кошка.

00:02:50.040 --> 00:02:53.740
In Russian fairy tales, the bear is often called Михаил Потапыч.

00:02:54.080 --> 00:02:56.640
He acts like a wise, but clumsy forest king.

00:02:57.300 --> 00:03:01.460
Russian have respect to bears for centuries, as symbols of strength and the deep woods.

00:03:02.020 --> 00:03:03.800
Do you remember what медведь means?

00:03:04.520 --> 00:03:07.040
Try using sabaka or кошка three times today.

00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:09.220
For kids, draw your favorite animal

00:03:09.220 --> 00:03:12.440
and say it's Russian name out loud three times while coloring.

00:03:12.940 --> 00:03:13.440
For adults?

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:16.000
Next time you see a dog or cat on the street,

00:03:16.320 --> 00:03:19.380
quietly say it's Russian name and make up one simple sentence.

00:03:20.060 --> 00:03:22.900
Now here's something really cool about one of the day's words.

00:03:23.380 --> 00:03:26.240
Did you know that медведь and the English word bear

00:03:26.240 --> 00:03:28.940
are actually cousins from the same ancient root?

00:03:29.540 --> 00:03:32.520
This word started long ago as something like bear

00:03:33.080 --> 00:03:34.700
and traveled through Slavic languages.

00:03:35.240 --> 00:03:38.220
It became медведь in Russian around the 11th century

00:03:38.220 --> 00:03:40.340
and literally means honey-eater.

00:03:41.140 --> 00:03:43.280
The Russian word sounds nothing like bear,

00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:45.580
yet both come from that hidden root

00:03:45.580 --> 00:03:48.100
that also gave us brown in some languages.

00:03:48.640 --> 00:03:50.300
Next time you see a teddy bear,

00:03:50.760 --> 00:03:52.860
remember it is cousins with медведь.

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:56.420
They both come from that ancient honey-eater idea

00:03:56.420 --> 00:04:00.380
and that connection is your secret shortcut to remembering it forever.

00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:02.860
Молодец, that means well done.

00:04:03.380 --> 00:04:05.860
Remember, every expert started as a beginner,

00:04:06.380 --> 00:04:09.380
practicing today's words out loud even just once

00:04:09.380 --> 00:04:11.640
and you'll be amazed how fast you learn.

00:04:11.940 --> 00:04:13.160
See you next time, poka.

00:04:13.620 --> 00:04:14.980
That's Russian for buy.

